  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has fern-like, deeply lobed leaves that can be used to teach about leaf morphology and plant adaptation. The leaves are evergreen, making it a good subject for lessons on different leaf life cycles. Its clusters of white flowers attract pollinators, offering a practical example of plant-pollinator interactions. The tree&#x27;s bark peels in strips, which can be used to discuss tree growth and bark functions.",
